{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790349524,"nonce":"uas7WgQclSYYj4t9nPYMf0kWdo0=","title":"A call to an undefined function inside a for body becomes an indirect call through an integer","message":"def main() {\n        for i in range(0, 5) {\n            nosuch(i)\n        }\n    }\n\n`zynml run` segfaults (status 139) and `zyntax compile --backend llvm` fails with \"Code generation error: Expected function type for indirect call, got: I64\". The same call in a `while` body, or outside a loop, is the lowering error \"Call to undefined function 'nosuch'\". The SSA builder refuses an indirect call only when the callee value is Undef (crates/compiler/src/ssa.rs:5070); inside the counted for loop the unknown name most likely reads as the loop block's placeholder value rather than Undef, so the check passes and the call goes out as HirCallable::Indirect. crates/zynml/examples/test_09_for_loop.zynml hits this under zyntax compile, where `println` is unknown. Possibly the same shape as fb7a954. NUC x86_64, main 19697230.","files":null}]}